  "description_short": "Bright village café in Storms River serving fresh breakfasts, hearty lunches and homemade treats.",
  "description_long": "Tucked along Gammasi Street in the heart of Storms River village, Tsitrus Café brings a cheerful splash of colour and warmth to this adventure hub. The bright interior and welcoming atmosphere make it a natural gathering spot for hikers tackling the Otter Trail, travellers exploring Tsitsikamma, and locals catching up over coffee.\n\nThe menu covers all the bases with generous breakfasts, satisfying burgers and wraps, and daily specials that lean on fresh, honest ingredients. Their homemade cakes and baked goods are worth leaving room for, and the coffee keeps you fuelled for whatever the Garden Route throws at you next. It's the kind of place where service feels genuinely friendly rather than scripted, and portions don't leave you hungry an hour down the road.\n\nWhether you're stopping in before a forest walk or settling in after a day on the Bloukrans Bridge, Tsitrus Café delivers exactly what a village eatery should: good food, fair prices, and a welcoming space that feels like part of the community rather than just passing through it.",
